WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.020
Every living organism is made of cells.

2
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.380
Cells are the basic unit of life, the smallest units that can carry out all the

3
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.380
processes of life.

4
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.680
This connects living things that look very different.

5
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.340
Plants and animals are made of cells.

6
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.700
So are bacteria and archaea.

7
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.680
Their cells differ in size and shape, but cells are what they share.

8
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.623
Every new cell comes from a cell that already existed.

9
00:00:29.603 --> 00:00:31.663
New cells form when existing cells divide.

10
00:00:32.563 --> 00:00:36.663
The cell theory connects living things through cells, and explains where new cells

11
00:00:36.663 --> 00:00:37.663
come from.

12
00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.967
The cell theory has six ideas.

13
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:43.007
The other three explain what cells do and share.

14
00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:45.827
Metabolism happens inside cells.

15
00:00:46.707 --> 00:00:51.587
These chemical reactions include breaking down sugar to release energy for the cell

16
00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:55.267
to use. DNA carries hereditary information.

17
00:00:56.207 --> 00:00:58.707
When a cell divides, each new cell gets a copy.

18
00:00:59.887 --> 00:01:04.907
Cells also share the same main kinds of molecules: proteins, lipids, carbohydrates

19
00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:06.067
and nucleic acids.

20
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:09.927
The details differ, but the basic composition is shared.

21
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.057
How did scientists support these ideas?

22
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:17.257
Hooke's cork showed walls of dead cells in one plant material.

23
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:22.957
Scientists had to compare many plant and animal tissues to find the shared cellular

24
00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:28.397
plan. They also corrected a wrong idea: that new cells could form inside a

25
00:01:28.397 --> 00:01:29.397
structureless fluid.

26
00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:33.037
Remak published evidence that existing cells divide.

27
00:01:34.157 --> 00:01:36.837
Virchow spread the idea: every cell comes from a cell.

28
00:01:37.437 --> 00:01:42.637
A scientific theory is a well-tested explanation supported by many lines of

29
00:01:42.637 --> 00:01:45.737
evidence. It can change when new evidence arrives.

30
00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.047
Microscopes helped reveal the evidence.

31
00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:51.967
Magnification makes an image bigger.

32
00:01:53.227 --> 00:01:55.327
Resolution decides how much detail it holds.

33
00:01:56.287 --> 00:01:58.407
Enlarging a blur cannot add missing detail.

34
00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:00.547
Many cells are almost clear.

35
00:02:01.547 --> 00:02:04.547
Stains add contrast by sticking to some parts more than others.

36
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.840
An ordinary light microscope can show a cheek cell or a bacterium.

37
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.480
Ribosomes are too small for it to resolve.

38
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.300
Electron microscopes reveal finer details, including ribosomes.

39
00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:20.393
Tools made observations possible.

40
00:02:21.553 --> 00:02:25.453
Comparisons and evidence of division supported and corrected the theory.

41
00:02:26.333 --> 00:02:30.813
Its central idea connects all living things: cells are the basic units of life.
